<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Akaki Chkhenkeli</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1874–1959</span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Akaki Chkhenkeli was a Georgian Menshevik politician who headed the government of the short-lived Transcaucasian Democratic Federative Republic in April–May 1918 and led its delegation in peace talks with the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ottoman-empire">Ottoman Empire</a>. After the federation dissolved he served as foreign minister of the Democratic Republic of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/georgia">Georgia</a>, and he went into exile in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a> after the Soviet invasion of 1921.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/akaki-chkhenkeli.jpg" alt="Akaki Chkhenkeli" width="320" height="435" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown authorUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Chkhenkeli_AI.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
